# PuralvOS task set
#
# What PuralvOS installs, and nothing else.
#
# This list is not invented. It is the Ubuntu Studio Installer's own task table,
# taken from backend.py in ubuntustudio-installer 2.0.7 (stonking):
#
#     METAPACKAGES = (
#         "ubuntustudio-lowlatency-settings",
#         "ubuntustudio-performance-tweaks",
#         "ubuntustudio-audio",
#         "ubuntustudio-graphics",
#         "ubuntustudio-photography",
#         "ubuntustudio-publishing",
#         "ubuntustudio-video",
#         "ubuntustudio-wallpapers",
#         "ubuntustudio-menu",
#         "ubuntu-edu-music",
#     )
#
# PuralvOS is that list minus photography and publishing. Everything else is
# carried over unchanged, because the upstream tasks are curated by people who
# know which combination of applications actually cooperates with PipeWire,
# which plugins build, and which plugin hosts need which libraries.
#
# Resolved against Ubuntu 26.10 (stonking), ubuntustudio-* 26.10.20.

# --- the three tasks that define the product -------------------------------

ubuntustudio-audio
ubuntustudio-video
ubuntustudio-graphics

# --- real time performance ------------------------------------------------
#
# The reason this is more than "Ubuntu with three boxes ticked".

ubuntustudio-lowlatency-settings
ubuntustudio-performance-tweaks

# --- session and shell integration ----------------------------------------

ubuntustudio-default-settings
ubuntustudio-menu
ubuntustudio-pipewire-config

# --- kernel ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The real time kernel, taken from the Ubuntu archive. No PPA, which matters
# twice over: PPAs need apt pinning to work at all, and they are the usual way
# a system ends up holding a kernel nobody will ever patch.
#
# linux-realtime, NOT linux-lowlatency. On Ubuntu 26.04 these are not what the
# names suggest, and picking the wrong one fails silently:
#
#     linux-lowlatency   Depends: linux-image-generic (= 7.0.0-14.14)
#                        "Complete Generic Linux kernel and headers with
#                         lowlatency boot configuration"
#
#     linux-realtime     Depends: linux-image-realtime (= 7.0.0-14.14.1)
#                        "Complete Linux kernel for real-time systems"
#
# linux-lowlatency is the GENERIC kernel with low latency boot arguments:
# mitigations off, no watchdog, that sort of thing. It still preempts
# cooperatively, so it will still glitch under audio load. linux-realtime is
# the PREEMPT_RT build, which is what real time priority actually needs.
#
# Verified against the resolute archive, not assumed. tools/kernel-select.py
# re-derives this at build time so an upstream rename cannot quietly put a
# generic kernel on a machine that thinks it has a real time one:
#
#     tools/kernel-select.py --policy realtime
#
# NOTE: the stock Ubuntu Studio ISO does NOT ship this kernel. Its manifest
# carries only linux-generic 7.0.0-14.14. The real time kernel is installed
# into the installed system by the installer, so PuralvOS has to do it
# explicitly or it will silently be a general kernel.

linux-realtime

# --- deliberately absent --------------------------------------------------
#
# Not in this list, on purpose:
#
#   ubuntustudio-photography   darktable and friends; PuralvOS is audio, video
#                              and graphics
#   ubuntustudio-publishing    scribus, calibre and a document suite; not
#                              media production
#   ubuntustudio-wallpapers    optional, kept out so the image carries only
#                              what does work
#   ubuntu-edu-music           music education classroom tools; revisit if
#                              PuralvOS grows an education story
#   ubuntu-studio-desktop      THE umbrella. Installing it is how a media
#                              workstation turns into a general desktop with
#                              LibreOffice, snapd, synaptic and printer drivers
#                              in it. Never install it here; see excludes.list.
